  "instructions": [
    "Bring the rice, water, and 1/2 tsp of the kosher salt from the kofta amount to a boil in a medium pot. Cover, reduce to low, and cook 15 minutes until the water is absorbed.",
    "Heat a grill or grill pan to medium-high, about 450 F. Brush the grates with a little oil.",
    "In a large bowl, mix the lamb, onion, garlic, parsley, cumin, coriander, cinnamon, remaining salt, and pepper. Mix gently until just combined.",
    "Divide the meat into 8 portions. Shape each into a 4-inch log about 1 inch thick, pressing firmly so it holds together.",
    "Brush the kofta with 1 tbsp olive oil. Grill 10 to 12 minutes, turning every 3 minutes, until browned and a thermometer reads 160 F.",
    "While the kofta cook, stir 1/4 cup olive oil, the lemon juice, and the mint together in a small bowl for the sauce.",
    "Fluff the rice with a fork. Divide it among four plates and top with the kofta and cucumber slices.",
    "Spoon the lemon herb sauce over the kofta and rice. Serve right away."
  ],
